GameBox optional mouse-look patch for doomgeneric
=================================================

Stock doomgeneric does not read the mouse. The GameBox native bridge
(doomgeneric_gamebox.c) exports `DG_GetMouse(int*dx,int*dy,int*buttons)` and the
Java side pushes relative motion with `gamebox_doom_push_mouse(...)`. To make
DOOM actually turn/fire from the mouse, wire that hook into the engine's
per-tic command builder.

Apply conceptually to doomgeneric/doomgeneric/g_game.c, inside G_BuildTiccmd():

    extern int DG_GetMouse(int* dx, int* dy, int* buttons);   // add near top

    // ... inside G_BuildTiccmd(), after the keyboard/joystick section:
    {
        int mdx = 0, mdy = 0, mbtn = 0;
        if (DG_GetMouse(&mdx, &mdy, &mbtn))
        {
            // Horizontal mouse -> turn (same scaling DOOM uses for mouse).
            cmd->angleturn -= (mdx * 0x8) & 0xFFFF;

            // Buttons: bit0 = fire, bit1 = use.
            if (mbtn & 1) cmd->buttons |= BT_ATTACK;
            if (mbtn & 2) cmd->buttons |= BT_USE;

            // (mdy is available for mouselook / forward if desired.)
        }
    }

Build order:
  1. ./build.sh clones doomgeneric into native/doomgeneric.
  2. Apply the edit above to native/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/g_game.c.
  3. Re-run `make DOOMGENERIC_DIR=doomgeneric/doomgeneric install-mod`.

Without this patch, GameBox DOOM is fully playable with the keyboard
(WASD move/strafe, arrows, Ctrl = fire, Space = use, Enter/Esc for menus); the
mouse deltas are simply ignored by the engine.
